    "https://hr.utk.edu/staff-positions/": {
      "title": "Staff Positions",
      "description": "Staff Positions | Human Resources Skip to content Skip to main navigation Report an accessibility issue The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Toggle navigation MENU Toggle navigation CLOSE Home About Back About Office Location Staff Job Seekers Back Job Seekers Staff Positions Dual Career Program Executive Search Meet the Executive Search Team Recent Placements Executive Positions Dual Career Program Temporary Employment Faculty Positions New Vol Onboarding Back New Vol Onboarding New VOL Onboarding 946-CARE Back 946-CARE 946-CARE for Distressed Faculty and Staff HR Employee Hub Back HR Employee Hub HR Employee Hub Human Resources Staff Positions Advantages and Benefits Staff Positions for External Candidates Staff Positions for Internal Candidates Employees are the university’s greatest asset and are critical to its ability to achieve success in classrooms, communities, and offices. Whether you’re a current UT employee looking to make a change, or you are considering a career at the university for the first time, we invite you to explore our openings and find your place in the UT family. To assist with your career search, UT offers an online application that enables you to search and apply for positions. Through this system, you can: View and apply for job postings online securely. Maintain an online employment application and track the status of the positions for which you have applied; and Search and apply for positions from any location with internet access at any time. HR wishes you success in your career journey. Please email [email protected] for assistance. UT Knoxville is committed to providing a positive and accessible candidate experience for all. For accommodation requests, please visit the Equal Opportunity & Accessibility website or contact the office at 865-974-2498 or via email at [email protected] . Why Work at UT? As a member of the UT family, you’ll be surrounded by top-notch faculty, staff, and students from around the world. In Knoxville, you’ll have plenty of opportunities to experience delicious food, great entertainment, and fun outdoor adventures. On campus, you’ll be part of a community that is passionate about changing the world and cheering for its elite SEC athletes. Benefits At the University of Tennessee, we strive to provide our staff members with a comprehensive suite of benefits . Please review the Summary of Benefits . For complete information about insurance, retirement, and other benefits available to you as regular staff, please visit the UT System HR Benefits page for more information. Discover Knoxville Vols call Knoxville home, sweet home. It’s the city where our campus stands proudly beside the Tennessee River and amidst the excitement of downtown. Enjoy easy access to outdoor activities and of course The Great Smoky Mountains National Park! Get to know the city and surrounding areas and understand why Vols love it here! The University of Tennessee Accolades UT has numerous awards including Dream Employer, Best Employer for New Graduates, and more! UT supports a healthy work-life balance and UT Knoxville employees agree. Recruiting, hiring, and retaining service members, military veterans, and their families is a priority for UT. Bronze Badge recipient for 2025 and 2026. UT offers meaningful benefits that help employees balance their professional and family lives. Thank you for your interest in a career with the University of Tennessee. We are excited for you to learn more about becoming a part of the UT Family. As you explore our many employment opportunities, we encourage you to remain vigilant against recruitment scams designed to target job seekers. The University of Tennessee will never ask you to provide money to accept a job offer or to participate in a search process. Please contact your campus Human Resources office if you have questions about the validity of a request or communication you receive relating to employment with the university. The University of Tennessee, Knoxville, is committed to the safety and security of the campus community. As required by the Clery Act, the university releases an Annual Security & Fire Safety Report addressing a wide range of safety information and security procedures. This report contains information regarding topics such as crime reporting, crime prevention and awareness programming, fire safety, a university police overview, emergency response, disciplinary procedures, and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. The report also contains information for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the university, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. You may download the report at tiny.utk.edu/ASFSR or request a hard copy by emailing [email protected] . Additional Resources Title IX Benefits, Retirement, Payroll, & Insurance Notice of Alien Labor Certifications Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B Employees Employee News Forbes Recognizes UT Among Tennessee’s Best Employers Turfgrass Research Making Headlines Around the World UT Knoxville Advisory Board To Meet May 12 Contact Us Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. EST 865-974-6642 | [email protected] CONCERNED ABOUT AN EMPLOYEE? Distressed Faculty and Staff Hotline 865-946-CARE (865-946-2273) Human Resources Cherokee Mills 2220 Sutherland Ave, Ste 220 Knoxville, TN 37919 Phone: 865-974-6642 Email: [email protected] Facebook LinkedIn The University of Tennessee, Knoxville The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Knoxville, Tennessee 37996 865-974-1000 Search for: Events A-Z Apply Privacy Map Directory Give to UT Accessibility The flagship campus of the University of Tennessee System and partner in the Tennessee Transfer Pathway ."
    },
    "https://hr.utk.edu/dual-career-program/": {
      "title": "Dual Career Program",
      "description": "Dual Career Program | Human Resources Skip to content Skip to main navigation Report an accessibility issue The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Toggle navigation MENU Toggle navigation CLOSE Home About Back About Office Location Staff Job Seekers Back Job Seekers Staff Positions Dual Career Program Executive Search Meet the Executive Search Team Recent Placements Executive Positions Dual Career Program Temporary Employment Faculty Positions New Vol Onboarding Back New Vol Onboarding New VOL Onboarding 946-CARE Back 946-CARE 946-CARE for Distressed Faculty and Staff HR Employee Hub Back HR Employee Hub HR Employee Hub Human Resources Dual Career Program The Dual Career Program (DCP) supports partners of newly hired University of Tennessee, Knoxville employees by providing tools, resources, and guidance for finding employment in the Knoxville area. The program helps connect participants with potential employment opportunities and assists them as they navigate the local job market. We recognize that career decisions are made within the context of personal and family needs. The DCP reflects the University’s commitment to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified workforce. The Dual Career Program provides consultative support but cannot guarantee employment with the University or any community partners. Eligibility for the Dual Career Program: Partners of full-time UT employees who relocate to the Knoxville area are eligible for Dual Career Program services for up to two years following their hire date, regardless of when their relocation occurs. What Services are Offered? One-on-one consultations Application and resume review Interview coaching Local career guidance such as: Networking events Career Fairs Professional development opportunities Personalized sourcing for career opportunities within UT, Knoxville Additional resources can be discussed with recruiter during consultation Why Dual Career Program? Support – Receive personalized job search assistance to jumpstart your career in the Knoxville area. Resources – Access expert guidance on resumes, applications, and local job leads Transition – Make your move to Knoxville smoother with dedicated career support Networking – Connect with local employers and opportunities through UT partnerships. Get Started To schedule a consultation, please complete the Dual Career Inquiry Form and a recruiter will follow up with you within two business days. Dual Career Recruitment Collaborators Companies and recruitment teams can receive information about talented professionals from UT Knoxville’s Dual Career Program. Get introduced to qualified candidates seeking new career opportunities as they transition to Knoxville, Tennessee. Become a Recruitment Collaborator Explore Participant Testimonials “The Dual Career Office was an incredible resource for me as I navigated the application and interview process for UTK. I was able to work one-on-one with a career coach who offered me invaluable resources for interview preparation, as well as information about the UTK system and culture. It was also nice to have a point person in the Dual Career Office that I could refer to if I had questions about the application process (Anthony was great!).” – Erika Sengstack – Service Coordinator, UTK “My experience with the Dual Career Program at the University of Tennessee, Knoxville has been extremely positive. From the start, the team’s support with resume help and application guidance made my job search remarkably smooth during a busy time. Their responsiveness made our transition to Knoxville less stressful and helped me find meaningful employment and I’m truly grateful for their commitment to supporting dual-career families.” – Mary Beth Barnes – Academic Advisor, UTK ““I want to take a moment to express my sincere appreciation for the Dual Career Program at UTK and the support they provided. Their guidance and resources have been incredibly helpful in assisting with job opportunities that made our transition to Knoxville remarkably smooth and less stressful.” – Chandrani Das – Administrative Specialist III Additional Resources Title IX Benefits, Retirement, Payroll, & Insurance Notice of Alien Labor Certifications Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B Employees Employee News Forbes Recognizes UT Among Tennessee’s Best Employers Turfgrass Research Making Headlines Around the World UT Knoxville Advisory Board To Meet May 12 Contact Us Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. EST 865-974-6642 | [email protected] CONCERNED ABOUT AN EMPLOYEE? Distressed Faculty and Staff Hotline 865-946-CARE (865-946-2273) Human Resources Cherokee Mills 2220 Sutherland Ave, Ste 220 Knoxville, TN 37919 Phone: 865-974-6642 Email: [email protected] Facebook LinkedIn The University of Tennessee, Knoxville The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Knoxville, Tennessee 37996 865-974-1000 Search for: Events A-Z Apply Privacy Map Directory Give to UT Accessibility The flagship campus of the University of Tennessee System and partner in the Tennessee Transfer Pathway ."
    },
    "https://hr.utk.edu/executive-search/executive-positions/": {
      "title": "Executive Positions",
      "description": "Executive Positions | Human Resources Skip to content Skip to main navigation Report an accessibility issue The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Toggle navigation MENU Toggle navigation CLOSE Home About Back About Office Location Staff Job Seekers Back Job Seekers Staff Positions Dual Career Program Executive Search Meet the Executive Search Team Recent Placements Executive Positions Dual Career Program Temporary Employment Faculty Positions New Vol Onboarding Back New Vol Onboarding New VOL Onboarding 946-CARE Back 946-CARE 946-CARE for Distressed Faculty and Staff HR Employee Hub Back HR Employee Hub HR Employee Hub Human Resources Executive Positions Executive Director for Financial Strategy and Operations in the Division of Student Life The University of Tennessee, Knoxville invites applications for the Executive Director for Financial Strategy and Operations in the Division of Student Life. Reporting to the Vice Chancellor for Student Life and serving on the Student Life Executive Leadership Team, the Executive Director is the division’s senior financial and operational leader. The Executive Director provides strategic leadership for financial planning, budgeting, resource allocation, operational effectiveness, and technology strategy while serving as a trusted advisor to the Vice Chancellor. The position ensures sound financial stewardship, compliance, and alignment of resources with divisional priorities and student success goals and advances operational excellence and long-term organizational sustainability through collaboration with campus partners. The position provides oversight for a Student Life budget exceeding $90M to $100M and leadership for financial, technology, and administrative functions supporting the division. Interested candidates should review the full description and formally apply via our applicant portal . To be assured for full consideration please include a letter of intent, CV/Resume, and names and contact information for three (3) professional references on or before Sunday, October 18, 2026 . Nominations and confidential inquiries are encouraged and may be sent via e-mail to Anthony Lanagan, Executive Recruiter, at [email protected] . Director, Center for Financial Wellness, Office of Financial Aid and Scholarships The University of Tennessee, Knoxville, is seeking a Director of the Center for Financial Wellness. Reporting to the Assistant Vice Provost for Financial Aid, this position role includes full responsibility for the Center’s operations, including staffing, resource management, organizational development, and performance oversight. As the university’s primary financial wellness expert, the Director collaborates with senior leaders, academic departments, and campus partners to embed financial wellness throughout the student experience. Interested candidates should review the full description and formally apply via our applicant portal . To be assured for full consideration please include a letter of intent, CV/Resume, and names and contact information for three (3) professional references on or before Sunday, September 20, 2026 . Nominations and confidential inquiries are encouraged and may be sent via e-mail to Brooke M. Swart, Executive Search Manager at [email protected] . Thank you for your interest in the University of Tennessee, Knoxville. If you are interested in being considered for future opportunities, please complete this Executive Recruitment Interest Form so recruiters may reach out to you with leadership positions should they align with your experience and interests. Thank you for your interest in a career with the University of Tennessee. We are excited for you to learn more about becoming a part of the UT Family. As you explore our many employment opportunities, we encourage you to remain vigilant against recruitment scams designed to target job seekers. The University of Tennessee will never ask you to provide money to accept a job offer or to participate in a search process. Please contact your campus Human Resources office if you have questions about the validity of a request or communication you receive relating to employment with the university. The University of Tennessee, Knoxville, is committed to the safety and security of the campus community. As required by the Clery Act, the university releases an Annual Security & Fire Safety Report addressing a wide range of safety information and security procedures. This report contains information regarding topics such as crime reporting, crime prevention and awareness programming, fire safety, a university police overview, emergency response, disciplinary procedures, and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. The report also contains information for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the university, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. You may download the report at tiny.utk.edu/ASFSR or request a hard copy by emailing [email protected] . Additional Resources Title IX Benefits, Retirement, Payroll, & Insurance Notice of Alien Labor Certifications Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B Employees Employee News Forbes Recognizes UT Among Tennessee’s Best Employers Turfgrass Research Making Headlines Around the World UT Knoxville Advisory Board To Meet May 12 Contact Us Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. EST 865-974-6642 | [email protected] CONCERNED ABOUT AN EMPLOYEE? Distressed Faculty and Staff Hotline 865-946-CARE (865-946-2273) Human Resources Cherokee Mills 2220 Sutherland Ave, Ste 220 Knoxville, TN 37919 Phone: 865-974-6642 Email: [email protected] Facebook LinkedIn The University of Tennessee, Knoxville The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Knoxville, Tennessee 37996 865-974-1000 Search for: Events A-Z Apply Privacy Map Directory Give to UT Accessibility The flagship campus of the University of Tennessee System and partner in the Tennessee Transfer Pathway ."
    },
    "https://hr.utk.edu/faculty-positions/": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Faculty Positions | Human Resources Skip to content Skip to main navigation Report an accessibility issue The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Toggle navigation MENU Toggle navigation CLOSE Home About Back About Office Location Staff Job Seekers Back Job Seekers Staff Positions Dual Career Program Executive Search Meet the Executive Search Team Recent Placements Executive Positions Dual Career Program Temporary Employment Faculty Positions New Vol Onboarding Back New Vol Onboarding New VOL Onboarding 946-CARE Back 946-CARE 946-CARE for Distressed Faculty and Staff HR Employee Hub Back HR Employee Hub HR Employee Hub Human Resources Faculty Positions UTK faculty members are central to the educational experiences of the undergraduate and graduate students. The Office of the Provost is committed to making UT a comfortable and supportive academic and research environment. Faculty Recruitment and Hiring UT System HR Benefits Website Internal Faculty Positions Thank you for your interest in a career with the University of Tennessee. We are excited for you to learn more about becoming a part of the UT Family. As you explore our many employment opportunities, we encourage you to remain vigilant against recruitment scams designed to target job seekers. The University of Tennessee will never ask you to provide money to accept a job offer or to participate in a search process. Please contact your campus Human Resources office if you have questions about the validity of a request or communication you receive relating to employment with the university. The University of Tennessee, Knoxville, is committed to the safety and security of the campus community. As required by the Clery Act, the university releases an Annual Security & Fire Safety Report addressing a wide range of safety information and security procedures. This report contains information regarding topics such as crime reporting, crime prevention and awareness programming, fire safety, a university police overview, emergency response, disciplinary procedures, and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. The report also contains information for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the university, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. You may download the report at tiny.utk.edu/ASFSR or request a hard copy by emailing [email protected] . Additional Resources Title IX Benefits, Retirement, Payroll, & Insurance Notice of Alien Labor Certifications Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B Employees Employee News Forbes Recognizes UT Among Tennessee’s Best Employers Turfgrass Research Making Headlines Around the World UT Knoxville Advisory Board To Meet May 12 Contact Us Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. EST 865-974-6642 | [email protected] CONCERNED ABOUT AN EMPLOYEE? Distressed Faculty and Staff Hotline 865-946-CARE (865-946-2273) Human Resources Cherokee Mills 2220 Sutherland Ave, Ste 220 Knoxville, TN 37919 Phone: 865-974-6642 Email: [email protected] Facebook LinkedIn The University of Tennessee, Knoxville The University of Tennessee, Knoxville Knoxville, Tennessee 37996 865-974-1000 Search for: Events A-Z Apply Privacy Map Directory Give to UT Accessibility The flagship campus of the University of Tennessee System and partner in the Tennessee Transfer Pathway ."
